# The headers of the frames that a Page sends: a 32-bit little-endian payload
# size, then a 32-bit little-endian type.
"\x04\x00\x00\x00\x01\x00\x00\x00"
"\x01\x00\x00\x00"
"\x02\x00\x00\x00"
"\x05\x00\x00\x00"
"\x06\x00\x00\x00"
"\x07\x00\x00\x00"
"\x08\x00\x00\x00"
"\x09\x00\x00\x00"
"\x0a\x00\x00\x00"
"\x0b\x00\x00\x00"
"\x0c\x00\x00\x00"
"\x11\x00\x00\x00"
"\x12\x00\x00\x00"
"\x13\x00\x00\x00"
"\x14\x00\x00\x00"
"\x15\x00\x00\x00"
"\x19\x00\x00\x00"
"\x1b\x00\x00\x00"
"\x09\x00\x00\x00\x05\x00\x00\x00"
"\x00\x00\x00\x01"
# What a result holds.
"Uncaught "
"null"
"\"\\ud800\""
"\xef\xbf\xbf"
# What a console message holds: a level from 1 to 5, then text.
"\x01"
"\x05"
"Uncaught (in promise) "
# What a request holds: a number, a kind from 1 to 2, then a URL, a method and
# header lines, each after its size, and a byte that says whether a body
# follows. A credit holds a number and up to 65536 bytes. A cancel holds a
# number.
"\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
"\x02"
"https://example.com/a.js"
"\x00\x00\x01\x00"
"\x03\x00\x00\x00GET"
"\x04\x00\x00\x00POST"
"X-Test: 1\x0a"
"Cookie: a=b\x0a"
"\x11\x00\x00\x00"
# What document.cookie may be set to.
"a=b; HttpOnly"
# What a CookieStore asks: a number, a byte that is 1 for all cookies, and a
# name; a cookie to set, with an expiry, a same-site byte from 1 to 3, a
# partitioned byte, then a name, a value and a domain, each after its size, and
# a path; whether to listen.
"\x00"
"\x03"
"__Host-"
".example.com"
"/"
# A BroadcastChannel's message: its name after its size, a byte that is 1 if it
# is locked to its agent cluster, and the bytes of the serialized value, which
# start with Blink's envelope and V8's header.
"\x04\x00\x00\x00news"
"\xff\x15\xfe"
"\xff\x0f"
# A document that the Page has made: its ID, a byte for its source, 0 for the
# initial about:blank and 1 for a navigation's response, and then the
# navigation's number. Each message of a document starts with its ID.
"\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
"\x02\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
